  "worked_solution": "Here, we convert the radical into a rational exponent, and we apply the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-5x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2/3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2/3})-5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{(\\frac{2}{3}-1)}-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-1/3}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{x}}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
